  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\int \\frac{d x}{x+x^7}=p(x)$ then, $\\int \\frac{x^6}{x+x^7} d x$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "02Bbe",
      "text": "\n$\\ln |x|-p(x)+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jjaB9",
      "text": "\n$\\ln |x|+p(x)+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "8LSLo",
      "text": "\n$x-p(x)+c$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CE3FY",
      "text": "\n$x+p(x)+c$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int \\frac{x^6}{x+x^7} d x=\\int \\frac{x^6}{x\\left(1+x^6\\right)} d x$\n$=\\int \\frac{\\left(1+x^6\\right)-1}{x\\left(1+x^6\\right)} d x$\n$=\\int \\frac{1}{x} d x-\\int \\frac{1}{x+x^7} d x$\n$=\\ln |x|-p(x)+c$",
    "image": null
  },
